From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of list_extract.cpp as used

list_extract.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (bound_function),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/list/list_extract.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/list/list_extract.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/list/list_extract.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/function/scalar/list/list_extract.cpp
@@ -125,6 +125,7 @@ static void ListExtractFunction(DataChunk &args, ExpressionState &state, Vector
 static unique_ptr<FunctionData> ListExtractBind(BindScalarFunctionInput &input) {
 	auto &context = input.GetClientContext();
 	auto &bound_function = input.GetBoundFunction();
+	(void)bound_function;
 	auto &arguments = input.GetArguments();
 	D_ASSERT(bound_function.GetArguments().size() == 2);
 	arguments[0] = BoundCastExpression::AddArrayCastToList(context, std::move(arguments[0]));
